 ### [Discrete Gaussian Curvature Estimation](14915-discrete-gaussian-curvature-estimation.md)
-This method classifies surface vertices as elliptic (local extrema) or hyperbolic (saddle/blending regions) by evaluating the sign of the discrete Gaussian curvature. It distinguishes itself from continuous curvature estimation by providing a robust Boolean classification based on the angular defect, which is computationally cheaper and less sensitive to noise than second-derivative approximations. It builds on [SDF Normal Estimation via Finite Differences](4619-sdf-normal-estimation-via-finite-differences.md) by offering a topological classification rather than directional magnitude.
